---Sliders provide the user with a method of selecting a value out of a configurable range, represented as a track with
---a draggable thumb indicator, with labels for the various values along the track, and a central label indicating the
---currently selected value.
---
---Similar to Carousels, there's also support for named entries, making them also useful for representing settings with
---multiple levels.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprites used for the thumb
---and track must represent a spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout.
---
---For the thumb the states are as follows: `default/neutral`, `mouseover`, `dragging`, `disabled`.
---
---And for the track the states are as follows: `default/enabled`, `default/enabled + filled region`, `disabled`,
---`disabled + filled region`.
---@class ui.Slider : ui.Component
---@field value integer The current value for the slider. Note modifying this triggers any potential value hooks set on this component, use `SetValue` instead if you need to skip those.
---@field valueLabel string (Read-only) The name of the entry associated with the currently selected value, or an empty string if the slider setup didn't include entry names.
---@field minValue integer (Read-only) The minimum value for this slider.
---@field maxValue integer (Read-only) The maximum value for this slider.
---@field numValues integer (Read-only) The number of values available on this slider. This takes into account `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `rate`.
---@field scale integer (Read-only) Divisor applied on the current value when displaying it, allowing integer values to be displayed as floating-point.
---@field rate integer (Read-only) The rate at which the slider transitions from `minValue` to `maxValue`. Also used to determine how often notches get displayed on the slider's track.
---@field labelsText ui.TextData (Read-only) (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying this slider's text labels.
---@field thumbSprite ui.SpriteData (Read-only) (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the slider's draggable thumb indicator.
---@field trackSprite ui.SpriteData (Read-only) (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the slider's track.
---@field notchSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the notches on the slider's track.
ui.Slider = {}

---Creates a new slider on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this slider in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.Slider # The newly created slider. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.Slider.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Configures the value range for this slider and its current value, returning true if the provided data represents a
---valid range for a slider.
---@param max integer Maximum value for this slider. Must be higher than `min`.
---@param curValue integer Current value for this slider. Must be between `min` and `max`.
---@return boolean # True if setup was successful, indicating the slider now has a valid range and is ready to be used.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Slider, min: integer, max: integer, curValue: integer, valueDisplayDivisor: integer, incrementRate: integer): boolean
---@overload fun(self: ui.Slider, entries: string[], selectedValue?: integer): boolean
---@overload fun(self: ui.Slider, entriesMap: table<string, integer>, selectedValue?: integer): boolean
function ui.Slider:Setup(max, curValue) end

---Sets the current value for this slider.
---@param value integer Desired current value for this slider.
---@param triggerEvents? boolean Whether or not to emit `ONSELECTIONCHANGED` events for this change. Defaults to false.
---@return boolean # True if the provided value is representable by this slider and was set successfully, false otherwise.
function ui.Slider:SetValue(value, triggerEvents) end
